questions.question_text:
The graph of a relation $y = f(x)$ is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-3,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1) -- (0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.63:1.63, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {\x*\x*\x*\x - 2*\x*\x + 2});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the maximum number of times a horizontal line intersects this graph?
